138
00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:21.390
Fast fact number one, Company Picnic was the 100th episode of The Office.

139
00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:22.390
Yes.

140
00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:28.530
This was a very big deal for the network because it meant our show was now eligible for syndication.

141
00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.490
Which I didn't even know what that meant.

142
00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.350
I thought maybe we should explain it.

143
00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:32.750
Okay.

144
00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:33.150
Do.

145
00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:36.190
Because I remember when we hit 100, I was like, what's all the hullabaloo?

146
00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:36.710
Yeah, sure.

147
00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.250
We hit 100.

148
00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:37.770
That's cool.

149
00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:38.230
I know.

150
00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.090
Maybe, you know, we'll all go out to dinner or something.

151
00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:41.830
No.

152
00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:42.170
No.

153
00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.110
For the network, super big.

154
00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.710
They all showed up to the set.

155
00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:46.510
They did.

156
00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:48.330
They brought a cake.

157
00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:51.190
It was as big as like a poker table.

158
00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.310
It was humongous.

159
00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:53.150
It was.

160
00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:53.850
That's what she said.

161
00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.110
That's what she said.

162
00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.130
They brought champagne.

163
00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.690
But we couldn't drink it.

164
00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.350
No, because we had to go back to work.

165
00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:04.530
We actually only had 15 minutes with the cake, all said and told.

166
00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:05.950
It was on our lunch break.

167
00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:10.330
So if you wanted to eat, we had 30 minutes, photo with a cake, and then we had to like run

168
00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:10.850
out the door.

169
00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.890
Well, I remember Greg gave a very nice speech.

170
00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:14.330
He did.

171
00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.550
About what the 100 episodes had meant to him.

172
00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:17.930
Entertainment Tonight was there.

173
00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.110
All the press was there.

174
00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:20.510
I mean, this was a super big deal.

175
00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:20.910
Mm-hmm.

176
00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.370
Let's tell you why.

177
00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:28.890
When a show hits 100 episodes and goes into syndication, it means that the network can

178
00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:35.210
now start selling the show in a package to different places where they can rerun it.

179
00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.690
So it doesn't just run on NBC anymore.

180
00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.110
It gets on all the cable networks.

181
00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.930
Like Comedy Central, how it reruns on Comedy Central.

182
00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:44.450
Right.

183
00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:48.270
And guys, remember, this predates all streaming.

184
00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:49.090
Yes.

185
00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.330
So this was all kind of a cable thing.

186
00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.310
But this meant big money for the network.

187
00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:55.390
I didn't know that.

188
00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:59.310
But it makes sense because these other places pay them to have it.

189
00:08:59.430 --> 00:08:59.770
Yes.

190
00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:06.150
But what I think a lot of people don't know is that the actors do not cash in on this

191
00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:09.150
unless they are what is called profit participants.

192
00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:09.850
Oh, yeah.

193
00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:10.410
And guess what?

194
00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:10.890
We weren't.

195
00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:11.610
We were not.

196
00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:17.490
Now, our union, SAG, does negotiate a small fee for syndicated reruns.

197
00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.710
So it's very fun.

198
00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.390
You get checks, and they're great.

199
00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:22.090
They're great.

200
00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.330
But they have, you guys, this, like, cascading tier.

201
00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:25.810
So you get a check, and you're like, whoop-hoo.

202
00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.130
Then the next one's a little lower.

203
00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:28.070
Then it's a little lower.

204
00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.130
Then it's a little lower.

205
00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.150
Then it's a little lower.

206
00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.150
Then it's a little lower.

207
00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:31.770
Yes.

208
00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:32.970
And then it's for, like, $2.

209
00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.650
Well, you know that bar that they have called Residuals in Burbank?

210
00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.410
This is a famous bar, you guys.

211
00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:39.770
Yeah.

212
00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:44.650
So there's this bar called Residuals, and if you're an actor and you bring in a residual

213
00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:49.250
check that's under $1, they'll give you a free drink, and then they tack your check

214
00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:49.990
up on the wall.

215
00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:50.450
Yeah.

216
00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:56.850
I have a friend of mine who saved a residual check for, I think it was $0.17, and I put it

217
00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:57.810
on his bulletin board.

218
00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.730
Lady, I got one for $0.21.

219
00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.850
It costs more money to mail it.

220
00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:02.430
I know.

221
00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:02.810
To me.

222
00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:03.790
Probably.

223
00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:04.750
And to print it.

224
00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:05.350
Yeah.

225
00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:06.670
Yeah, exactly.

226
00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:11.270
So yeah, they were able to make a lot of money selling the show to cable, and then eventually

227
00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:15.130
you guys, I mean, you know, they were able to sell it to all the streamers.

228
00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:15.650
Yeah.

229
00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:20.530
I guess we should probably say the actors don't get a big payout for that either.

230
00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.370
That money goes to the profit participants.

231
00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:29.470
See, the word profit participant is something I'd never heard of, and as it turns out, if you're

232
00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:32.450
one of those folks, that is the shiitake.

233
00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:33.510
Mm-hmm.

234
00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:34.350
Mm-hmm.

235
00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:35.170
Mm-hmm.

